    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d945">

                <pb facs="1092" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley
                    Files</note>
                <head>No. 945<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d945-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-29">July 29, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Clayton</hi>: I have your memorandum of July 28<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d945-f2"/> suggesting that we might concur in the recommendation
                    concerning certain questions regarding restitution of art objects, as
                    recommended by the Headquarters, U. S. Group Control Council.</p>
                <p>At your suggestion I have prepared a joint memorandum<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d945-f3"/> and have indicated my approval of it by my signature
                    thereon. If it meets with your approval I presume you will transmit the same to
                        General Clay for appropriate
                    action.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin W.
                                Pauley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
